      "text": "To determine the cost of the gas used for Ryosuke's automobile when he drives his friend back home, we first need to calculate the total distance driven. The odometer readings were 74,568 miles when Ryosuke picked up his friend and 74,592 miles when he dropped his friend off, giving a total distance driven of:\n\n\\[ 74,592 - 74,568 = 24 \\text{ miles} \\]\n\nNext, we need to determine the amount of gasoline used for this distance. Given that the car's fuel efficiency is 28 miles per gallon, the amount of gasoline used is:\n\n\\[ \\frac{24 \\text{ miles}}{28 \\text{ miles per gallon}} = \\frac{24}{28} \\text{ gallons} = \\frac{6}{7} \\text{ gallons} \\]\n\nNow, we need to calculate the cost of the gasoline used. The price of one gallon of gas is $4.05$. Therefore, the cost of the gas used is:\n\n\\[ \\frac{6}{7} \\times 4.05 = \\frac{6 \\times 4.05}{7} = \\frac{24.30}{7} = 3.471428571428571 \\approx 3.47 \\]\n\nSo, the cost of the gas used to drive Ryosuke's friend back home is:\n\n\\[ \\boxed{3.47} \\]",
